{#
    Shell for the public redemption pages.

    It carries no navigation on purpose — a visitor here has no account yet, so there is nowhere
    to navigate — which is why it is a centred column on the theme's canvas rather than the
    sidebar shell the signed-in sections use.

    US-01.14: the trainer's colour and logo *do* reach these pages. `_branding.html.twig` resolves
    branding from the share link's organization for an anonymous visitor, so somebody following a
    coach's invitation arrives on that coach's trainer's colours rather than on the platform's.
#}
{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block body_class %}pp-theme{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    {% set branding = viewer_branding() %}
    {% set logoUrl = branding_logo_url(branding) %}

    <main id="main-content" class="pp-public">
        {#
            The mark is not a link: there is nowhere on this site a visitor without an account is
            being invited to go. It names whose invitation this is, which is the question a
            redemption page has to answer before it asks for anything.
        #}
        <p class="pp-public-brand">
            {% if logoUrl %}
                <img src="{{ logoUrl }}" alt="">
            {% else %}
                {{ include('_logo.html.twig') }}
            {% endif %}
            <span>{{ branding.organizationName ?? app_name }}</span>
        </p>

        <div role="status" aria-live="polite">
            {% for label, messages in app.flashes %}
                {% for message in messages %}
                    <p class="flash flash-{{ label }}">{{ message }}</p>
                {% endfor %}
            {% endfor %}
        </div>

        <h1>{% block heading %}{% endblock %}</h1>

        <div class="pp-content">
            {% block join_content %}{% endblock %}
        </div>
    </main>
{% endblock %}
